# ===== verdict =====
# Gate 0 FAILS, on one pre-registered condition: no aie_trace* file was written. Every other condition holds.
#   - xdp_aie_trace_plugin.dll loaded from the SDK dir through AMD_NPU_SDK_PATH, by configuration alone.
#   - The outputs are bit-equal to the untraced arm on all 7 cases.
#   - The cached xmodel is unchanged (sha256 and mtime), so there was no recompile.
#   - The device was idle before and after both arms.
# Cause (stated by XRT itself, not inferred): "AIE metadata read failed!" and "AIE Metadata is empty for AIE
# Trace". The plugin looked for the AIE metadata JSON in the run directory. xdp_core.dll names the file
# aie_control_config.json. The overlay xclbin does carry an AIE_METADATA section (xclbinutil --info), but on
# this client path the plugin did not take it from there.
# Not tested here: supplying that metadata file. That would be a new pre-registered attempt (Gate 0b).
